      "role": "assistant",
      "reasoning": "The learner has identified one accepted place correctly but has not supplied the second. I should acknowledge that specific answer, clarify the one-mark-per-place scoring, and provide a concise model answer with other accepted options.",
      "content": "Mrs Mkize’s place in Alexandra is one correct answer, worth **1 mark**. You need one more distinct place for the full 2 marks.\n\n**Model answer:** Stephen Kumalo looked for Absalom at **Mrs Mkize’s place in Alexandra** and **the textile factory in Doornfontein**.\n\nOther accepted choices for the second place include **Mrs Ndlela’s place in Sophiatown, Hlatshwayos (Shanty Town), Pimville,** or **the reformatory**.\n\n### 📖 Concept & Thought Process (How to Understand It):\n* **The Concept / Rule:** For a question that says **“State TWO”**, give two separate details from the text. Each correct place earns one mark.\n* **The Thought Process (How to Unpack It):** Look for the places named in Kumalo’s account of searching for Absalom. Choose two different places and state them clearly.\n* **How DBE Markers Score It:** **1 mark for each correct place**, up to 2 marks. You do not need to explain your choices.\n\n🎯 **Exam Tip:** Make sure your two answers are distinct. A vague answer or repeating the same place will not earn the second mark."
